This also happens with the UTf8JsonReader with the same underlying issue:
```csharp
var jsonBytes = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(@"""\u001c\u0001""");
var reader = new Utf8JsonReader(jsonBytes);
reader.Read();
reader.TryGetDateTime(out var datetime);
```
From my investigation the issue is that escaped string fool some of the string length validation in [TryGetDateTimeCore](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/libraries/System.Text.Json/src/System/Text/Json/Reader/Utf8JsonReader.TryGet.cs#L1075), but further down the `Unescape` call reduces the data length to less then 10 bytes.

This should happen regardless of if the value is in  `ValueSpan` or a `ValueSequence`
